From: Playtendoh
Subject: [PATCH] Angrylion: room for 16 workers, not 64

rdp.c keeps a 574 KiB rdp_state for each worker it could have, 35 MiB of the app's image (.bss) for
64. Playtendoh runs 6 (parallel-n64-angrylion-multithread), on a PS5's 13 CPUs; parallel_alinit
already holds a larger count to the most.

---
diff --git a/mupen64plus-video-angrylion/parallel_al.h b/mupen64plus-video-angrylion/parallel_al.h
index 5037195..a8a1c52 100644
--- a/mupen64plus-video-angrylion/parallel_al.h
+++ b/mupen64plus-video-angrylion/parallel_al.h
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@ extern "C" {
 
 #include <stdint.h>
 
-#define PARALLEL_MAX_WORKERS 64u
+/* PS5: Playtendoh runs 6 workers (port/libretro/game.cpp) on 13 CPUs; each slot is a 574 KiB
+   rdp_state in the app's image (.bss), and 64 of them were 35 MiB of it */
+#define PARALLEL_MAX_WORKERS 16u
 
 void parallel_alinit(uint32_t num);
 
